      "title": "‘New kind of cyber incident’: OpenAI apologises for Medicare hack and reveals extent of attack",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/29/openai-apology-rogue-agent-hacked-medicare-australian-government-websites",
      "description": "<p>Chief strategy officer to fly to Australia to front joint committee on AI after breaches of government websites</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/29/treasurer-jim-chalmers-reserve-bank-cash-rate-decision-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>OpenAI has apologised to Australians for its <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/24/openai-agent-hacked-medicare-australia-what-we-know-so-far-ntwnfb\">agent attack on Medicare</a>, and will front parliament next week, as the tech company revealed more details about its June hack of Australian government websites.</p><p>In a <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/how-we-will-do-better-for-australia/\">blog post</a> released on Tuesday, OpenAI said it should have handled its response better.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/sep/29/openai-apology-rogue-agent-hacked-medicare-australian-government-websites\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T02:51:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australia news live: Shoebridge doesn’t rule himself out of Greens leadership race; UNSW’s warning after ‘drunk’ AI study",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/29/treasurer-jim-chalmers-reserve-bank-cash-rate-decision-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow the day’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>New South Wales police say they are investigating the suspicious deaths of two men in the state’s north.</p><p>Police said they found the first man – who has since been identified as a 79-year-old – dead at a property on Summerland Way at Gurranang, near Grafton, on 13 September.</p><p>And that’s equally important in the Reserve Bank’s mandate, dual mandate, which talks about maintaining full employment at the same time as they go for price stability, which means inflation in the target band.</p><p>Well, it’s still lower than what we saw under Howard and Costello, is the first point.</p><p>I think that’s pretty clear. And what we’ve seen in recent years is that it’s possible to have low and steady unemployment at the same time as we see inflation moderate to more normal levels.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/29/treasurer-jim-chalmers-reserve-bank-cash-rate-decision-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T02:49:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Looked like dried blood’: worker tells Beau Lamarre-Condon trial about finding suspicious belongings in skip",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/beau-lamarre-condon-murder-trial-greenkeeper-evidence-luke-davies-jesse-baird-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Former Sydney police officer, 31, has pleaded not guilty to murdering AFL umpire Jesse Baird and flight attendant Luke Davies</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/29/treasurer-jim-chalmers-reserve-bank-cash-rate-decision-coalition-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Brand new AFL shorts, a Qantas card and other bloodied belongings were found in a dumpster two days after football umpire Jesse Baird and flight attendant Luke Davies were allegedly murdered, a Sydney court has heard.</p><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon, 31, has been accused of fatally shooting the couple with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/29/beau-lamarre-condon-murder-trial-greenkeeper-evidence-luke-davies-jesse-baird-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T01:28:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Investigation of alleged gang-rape at Cornell University fraternity house reopened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/28/cornell-fraternity-investigation-alleged-gang-rape",
      "description": "<p>Outrage over treatment of alleged offenders, members of Chi Phi fraternity, has grown since lawsuit was made public</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for the Breaking News US newsletter email</a></p></li></ul><p>Prosecutors in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york\">New York</a> said on Monday that they have reopened an investigation into the alleged gang-rape of a student at Cornell University after an outcry over “leniency” shown to seven fraternity members named as the perpetrators.</p><p>According to lawyers for the student, who filed <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/newyork/news/cornell-university-lawsuit-fraternity-rape-allegations/\">a civil lawsuit</a> against the university and her alleged attackers earlier in September, only two members of the Chi Phi fraternity were expelled after the October 2024 incident, in which she said she was drugged and repeatedly raped over the course of seven hours.</p><p><em>Information and support for anyone affected by rape or sexual abuse issues is available from the following organizations. In the US, <a href=\"https://www.rainn.org/\">Rainn</a> offers support on 800-656-4673. In the UK, <a href=\"https://rapecrisis.org.uk/\">Rape Crisis</a> offers support on 0808 500 2222. In Australia, support is available at <a href=\"https://www.1800respect.org.au/\">1800Respect</a> (1800 737 732). Other international helplines can be found at <a href=\"http://ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html\">ibiblio.org/rcip/internl.html</a></em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/28/cornell-fraternity-investigation-alleged-gang-rape\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-28T22:03:26"
    }
  ]
